        "original_id": "7a563c15-cf7f-5f8a-a031-390611c84b32",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Reginald Engelbach\n- Places: Cairo, Harageh, Egypt\n- Organizations: Egyptian Museum of Cairo\n- Roles: Egyptologist, engineer\n- Projects: Register of museum artifacts, Harageh cemetery excavations\n\nFacts:\n- Reginald Engelbach was born on July 9, 1888, and he was an English Egyptologist and engineer.\n- Reginald Engelbach excavated the cemeteries at Harageh in 1913.\n- Reginald Engelbach is mainly known for his work at the Egyptian Museum of Cairo, especially compiling a register of the museum's artifacts.\n- Cairo is the capital and largest city of Egypt.\n- Reginald Engelbach died on February 26, 1946.",
